[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-47", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 47 — the count pushed into the lookup; IC05 112 ms; official schedule 1995.6 ops/s at TCR 0.00012", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-47.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 47 - the count pushed into the lookup; IC05 as one query; the official row 1361 -> 1996\n\n> Seed: iteration 46's S37 (IC05 under the schedule). Judge:\n> bench/benchmark.edn v2, `:schedule :official`; rung :sf1-full; SUT levi\n> (M4 4P+6E, 16 threads, 25.4M quads), driver judah, LAN.\n\n## Generate / Rank\n\n  IC05 spent its 161 ms materializing ~200k (forum, post) bindings to\n  produce 20 counts. datalog 9c86cc8d: COUNT PUSHDOWN -- when `:find`\n  wants exactly `(count ?e)` of the entity a last-clause composite binds\n  (?e in no other clause, not projected, the composite's value bound),\n  the lookup answers one binding per input weighted by its visible\n  entries, and `project`'s count sums weights. Tests: a hand count, a\n  hidden quad, and four shapes the pushdown must decline (value free,\n  entity reused, another variable, entity projected).\n\n  IC05 is now ONE query: `or-join [?person ?x]` over the two reaches (a\n  person in both is one ?x -- the union of two count queries would have\n  double-counted), the membership cut, the (creator, forum) composite,\n  `(count ?post)` pushed into it. Gate 4,780/0.\n\n    IC05, all 99 parameters, in-thread    p50      p90      max\n      iteration 45                        160.7    380.6    2301.6 ms\n      iteration 47                        111.7    261.2     388.0 ms\n\n    schedule official, 64 slots     tcr      on-time%  thru/s\n      it.46                         0.00015    96.18   1360.9\n      it.47                         0.00012   100.00   1995.6   (0.0001: 89.0% fails)\n\n  Read-after-write 477/0/0. Tests: datalog JVM 140/494/0, cljs 144/505/0;\n  kotobase-peer 263/808/0.\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - Three structures in three iterations from one query's profile: the\n    group order (35), composite lookups (45), weights (47). None is\n    IC05-specific; each is a shape the datom plane answers now.\n  - IC05 still costs 112 ms: the two-hop reach (2,200 persons) and\n    ~22k membership bindings before the counts. The official row moved\n    +47% because IC05 is paid 26 times a second under the schedule.\n  - The short-read generator (S38) remains the row's weakest\n    approximation and its largest lever.\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: GROWTH on the official column\n(1360.9 -> 1995.6, lowest passing TCR 0.00015 -> 0.00012). Ratio to the\naudited No.1: 70 on throughput at a 26x slower TCR.\n\nSeeds for iteration 48, in order:\n\n  - S38: the official short-read generator, exactly.\n  - S39: IC05's remaining 112 ms (the reach and the membership cut).\n  - S34: bindings as arrays. Owner: a SUT host.\n"}]
